  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that 3-Epi-20-Hydroxyecdysone may interact with Tankyrase-2 through a series of molecular targets, with the most direct link being through Tankyrase-2 as a downstream target of Thioredoxin, mitochondrial. This pathway is supported by two distinct routes: one involving 5-Oxobrucine and another involving 5-Hydroxy-2-Methylchromone-7-O-Rutinoside, both of which are targets of 3-Epi-20-Hydroxyecdysone. The shared involvement of Thioredoxin, mitochondrial in both paths indicates a potential common mechanism, possibly involving oxidative stress or redox regulation. The presence of multiple targets suggests that 3-Epi-20-Hydroxyecdysone may influence cellular processes through diverse pathways, with Tankyrase-2 being a key node in the network. The integration of these findings highlights the complexity of the relationship, emphasizing the role of Thioredoxin, mitochondrial in mediating the interaction between 3-Epi-20-Hydroxyecdysone and Tankyrase-2.",
